; IsaacRecomp mod. Turn it on or off with tools/mod_manager.html (or "mods =" in isaac.ini).
id = marksman
name = Marksman
version = 1.0
author = IsaacRecomp
category = HUD
summary = Completion marks for each character, as in Rebirth, and the challenge's goal on screen.
description = Your progress with each character, as Rebirth's completion marks. The character select gets one more note (in Eternal Edition between the hard mode note and Select!) with a mark for each ending - Mom (a footprint), Mom's Heart (a heart), Isaac (a cross), Satan (an upside-down cross) and ??? (a question mark); the original game has only Mom and Mom's Heart; a mark only appears once that boss has been met in some run, so nothing is spoiled -, for the character shown: faint until that character has reached it, written in once it has, red when it was in Eternal Edition's hard mode. The Gone has his own (with his mod on). An ending counts when its last boss is beaten (its room cleared) or the game shows it, in normal runs: not in challenges, Challenge Lab or with GenesisConsole on. Only endings reached with the mod on count (the game's save doesn't keep them by character). During a challenge (the game's and Challenge Lab's), the goal's mark is shown small in the HUD band, top left (with WideSaac's Hyper Zoom, in the top left corner). Kept in saves/marksman_<game>.txt. It only reads the game: runs play exactly the same with it on.

; options
; note = 1 shows the marks note on the character select (0: no)
note = 1
; challenge_goal = 1 shows the goal's mark during a challenge (0: no)
challenge_goal = 1
